WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.130 --> 00:00:02.480
- So the NRA, the
National Rifle Association

00:00:02.480 --> 00:00:04.220
has filed for bankruptcy,

00:00:04.220 --> 00:00:05.750
but before you get your hopes up,

00:00:05.750 --> 00:00:08.560
recognize that this is
Chapter 11 bankruptcy.

00:00:08.560 --> 00:00:11.510
A chapter 11 bankruptcy is
a kind of reorganization

00:00:11.510 --> 00:00:13.910
that attempts to pay off the creditors

00:00:13.910 --> 00:00:16.900
and allow the company or firm to continue

00:00:16.900 --> 00:00:18.590
as a going forward concern.

00:00:18.590 --> 00:00:20.300
Now, that being said, it can be used

00:00:20.300 --> 00:00:22.350
as a potential shield against litigation,

00:00:22.350 --> 00:00:23.890
or at least to delay litigation

00:00:23.890 --> 00:00:27.360
and the NRA has filed
for bankruptcy in Texas

00:00:27.360 --> 00:00:29.070
probably seeking a more favorable venue

00:00:29.070 --> 00:00:30.960
than New York where they're
currently being sued

00:00:30.960 --> 00:00:32.680
by Attorney General Tish James

00:00:32.680 --> 00:00:35.640
who has vowed to basically
sue them out of existence,

00:00:35.640 --> 00:00:37.250
but it will be interesting
to see what happens here,

00:00:37.250 --> 00:00:40.000
because the NRA is made up of
many different organizations,

00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:42.360
one of which the original
is chartered in New York,

00:00:42.360 --> 00:00:44.330
but those assets may be folded into

00:00:44.330 --> 00:00:46.430
some of the other NRA related affiliates.

00:00:46.430 --> 00:00:48.450
So the NRA is not going
anywhere at the moment.

00:00:48.450 --> 00:00:50.270
So stay tuned for more legal analysis

00:00:50.270 --> 00:00:51.753
and I'll see you in court.

